From: SP11 audio reconstruction <sp11-audio@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: honor DT disable-rfkill

The SP11 firmware reports the WCN7850 RF-kill GPIO with the wrong polarity,
leaving Wi-Fi hard-blocked. Allow board DT to suppress that unusable hardware
RF-kill path, matching the existing ACPI disable-rfkill policy.

This hook and the matching board property are required bake inputs: losing
either one disconnects the machine after boot and prevents remote development.

---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
index 980a12fb2c6e..18f9489a1233 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -80,6 +80,9 @@ static int ath12k_core_rfkill_config(struct ath12k_base *ab)
 	if (ath12k_acpi_get_disable_rfkill(ab))
 		return 0;
 
+	if (of_property_read_bool(ab->dev->of_node, "disable-rfkill"))
+		return 0;
+
	for (i = 0; i < ab->num_radios; i++) {
		ar = ab->pdevs[i].ar;
